From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] dagu: dri_flush must not block the compositor on throttle_fence

Against Mesa 26.0.8 (Ubuntu libgallium-26.0.8-1ubuntu0.3).

dri_flush() waits OS_TIMEOUT_INFINITE on drawable->throttle_fence
(previous swap). On dagu that fence is often implicit-synced to the
scanout BO. gnome-shell main sits in fence_finish / dri_flush for
65-80 ms inside clutter_frame_clock_dispatch, so the default-context
page-flip closure (notify_view / maybe_post) cannot run. Flip is on
time; the next kickoff waits for swap to return.

Zero timeout still entered a userspace wait loop on dagu. NOP the
fence_finish call; still drop the old fence via fence_reference.
GPU completion stays on the Cogl sync_fd / KMS path.

Live ELF (objdump-checked, r-xp 0x7ee8ea0000):
  0x1cf740  mov x3,#-1  ->  mov x3,#0
  0x1cf74c  blr x4      ->  nop

---
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_drawable.c
@@ -532,7 +532,7 @@ dri_flush(struct dri_context *ctx,
 
       /* throttle on the previous fence */
       if (drawable->throttle_fence) {
-         screen->fence_finish(screen, NULL, drawable->throttle_fence, OS_TIMEOUT_INFINITE);
+         screen->fence_finish(screen, NULL, drawable->throttle_fence, 0);
          screen->fence_reference(screen, &drawable->throttle_fence, NULL);
       }
       drawable->throttle_fence = new_fence;
